[medium] internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestions.go:147 (correctness)
If ResolveScope returns zero controls or zero label sets, PlannedCalls returns 0 but Generate still creates a pending DashboardSuggestionRun, creates no cells, and enqueues cellCount=0. Because active runs are unique per SSP while status is pending/running, this can leave an SSP with a pending run that has no worker cells to complete and blocks subsequent generate attempts with 409.
Suggested fix: Before creating the run, reject empty resolved scopes with a 422 response (for example when len(snapshot.ControlKeys)==0 or len(snapshot.LabelSetHashes)==0), or create a terminal completed/no-op run instead of a pending active run. Add an integration test for an SSP with no resolved controls and/or no label sets.
Guidance: Fix internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestions.go in DashboardSuggestionHandler.Generate. After svc.ResolveScope(...) and before generating runID/creating DashboardSuggestionRun, explicitly reject an empty resolved scope when len(snapshot.ControlKeys) == 0 or len(snapshot.LabelSetHashes) == 0. Return a client error, preferably 422 Unprocessable Entity, with a clear api.NewError message such as no controls resolved for dashboard suggestions or no evidence label sets resolved for dashboard suggestions. Do not enqueue with cellCount 0 and do not create a pending run with plannedCalls 0, because the active-run uniqueness for pending/running runs can block later generate requests. Keep the existing transaction/enqueue rollback behavior for non-empty scopes unchanged. Add an integration test in internal/api/handler/oscal/dashboard_suggestions_integration_test.go covering an SSP/scope that resolves zero controls and/or zero label sets: assert the response is 422, no dashboard_suggestion_runs row is created for that SSP, no cells are created, and a subsequent valid generate is not blocked by 409. Be careful not to treat the maxCallsPerRun check as sufficient; plannedCalls == 0 will not trip it.
